# standard.decimal.semsig — generated signature sidecar (README §16, §27).
# Exact fixed-point money/decimal math. `Decimal` is a scaled 64-bit integer,
# NOT a binary float — so 0.1 + 0.2 == 0.3 exactly and there is no representation
# error for currency. R-067: the runtime is now LOWERED at scale 2 (raw value =
# amount * 100): add/subtract/equal are scale-invariant integer ops; multiply
# divides the raw product by 100 and divide scales the dividend by 100, both
# truncating toward zero; overflow and divide-by-zero raise DecimalError (the
# fallible `catch`). X-093: Float operands into `decimal.*` (and Decimal/Money
# operands into Float `math.*`) are rejected (SS3093); `==`/`!=` on Float
# operands warn (SS3094).

decimalSig is semsig
decimalSig version "1.0"
decimalSig generatedBy "semanticscript 0.1"
decimalSig describes standard.decimal

Decimal is alias
Decimal for Int64
Decimal purpose "An exact fixed-point number (scaled Int64) for money/decimal math; never a binary float"

Money is alias
Money for Int64
Money purpose "An exact monetary amount in minor units (a Decimal specialized for currency)"

DecimalError is error
DecimalError purpose "Represent overflow / divide-by-zero / parse failures in exact decimal math"

decimalAdd is intrinsic
decimalAdd target decimal.add
decimalAdd arg left Decimal
decimalAdd arg right Decimal
decimalAdd out sum Decimal
decimalAdd catch DecimalError
decimalAdd purpose "Exact addition of two fixed-point decimals (R-067: lowered at scale 2, truncate toward zero)"

decimalSubtract is intrinsic
decimalSubtract target decimal.subtract
decimalSubtract arg left Decimal
decimalSubtract arg right Decimal
decimalSubtract out difference Decimal
decimalSubtract catch DecimalError
decimalSubtract purpose "Exact subtraction of two fixed-point decimals (R-067: lowered at scale 2, truncate toward zero)"

decimalMultiply is intrinsic
decimalMultiply target decimal.multiply
decimalMultiply arg left Decimal
decimalMultiply arg right Decimal
decimalMultiply out product Decimal
decimalMultiply catch DecimalError
decimalMultiply purpose "Exact multiplication with defined rounding (R-067: lowered at scale 2, truncate toward zero)"

decimalDivide is intrinsic
decimalDivide target decimal.divide
decimalDivide arg left Decimal
decimalDivide arg right Decimal
decimalDivide out quotient Decimal
decimalDivide catch DecimalError
decimalDivide purpose "Exact division with defined rounding; divide-by-zero is a DecimalError (R-067: lowered at scale 2, truncate toward zero)"

decimalEqual is intrinsic
decimalEqual target decimal.equal
decimalEqual arg left Decimal
decimalEqual arg right Decimal
decimalEqual out areEqual Bool
decimalEqual purpose "Exact equality of two fixed-point decimals (sound, unlike Float equality)"
